# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers: `scripts/omp_provider_repro.sh`
# is documented as a `docker run … bash /repro/…` command, and the fast-30
# workflow mounts these paths into the task image. A Windows checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` rewrote them to CRLF, which bash rejects
# (`$'\r': command not found`) before the first line of work — see the
# 2026-10-10 defect row in DEFECTS.md.
*.sh text eol=lf
